{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"745a2aed68ed4e0e","name":"card_event_commit_the_reserves","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/CovertOp/events/card_event_commit_the_reserves","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"COMMIT THE RESERVES","text":"Destroy target unit with attack equal or less than your kredit slots. Lose a kredit slot.","flavorText":"During WWII, the Japanese reserve system played a crucial role in mobilizing manpower for the war effort. The system consisted of several categories, including the first and second reserves, and the national guard, with an estimated total of 2.8 million men: approximately 1.3 million in the first reserve, 1 million in the second reserve, and half a million men in the national guard. Men who had completed their active duty service were assigned to these reserves and could be called up in times of need. However, as the war progressed and casualties mounted, the quality and training of reservists declined. Additionally, the Japanese military's focus on offensive tactics and its reluctance to rotate troops led to exhaustion and a lack of fresh reinforcements. This ultimately hampered Japan's ability to sustain its war effort and contributed to its eventual defeat.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_commit_the_reserves","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_commit_the_reserves_title","SourceString":"COMMIT THE RESERVES","LocalizedString":"COMMIT THE RESERVES"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_commit_the_reserves_text","SourceString":"Destroy target unit with attack equal or less than your kredit slots. Lose a kredit slot.","LocalizedString":"Destroy target unit with attack equal or less than your kredit slots. Lose a kredit slot."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_ev